# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Machine-local state
#
# Both are written on this machine by the installer and the UIs, and both hold
# absolute paths that mean nothing on anyone else's. gui_config.json is
# recreated on first launch (setup_lastools.py writes the LAStools path into
# it, and the app autodetects when it is missing); .fsct_setup is the stamp
# FSCT.bat compares against SETUP_VERSION to decide whether to rebuild the
# conda environment.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
gui_config.json
.fsct_setup

# wrapper_config.json is NOT ignored: it ships the default parameter set for
# batch_process.py and carries no machine-specific paths.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Downloaded dependencies
#
# ~150 MB, fetched and unpacked by setup_lastools.py (FSCT.bat lastools).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
third_party/LAStools/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pipeline output
#
# FSCT writes <input>_FSCT_output/ next to each input file, holding ~30 files
# and a few hundred MB per plot. All of it is reproducible from the input.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*_FSCT_output/
working_directory/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Point clouds
#
# Survey data does not belong in git - data/ alone is 2.9 GB here. The single
# exception is the benchmark file every timing in README.md and CHANGELOG.md is
# measured against, so a clone can reproduce those numbers.
#
# Note the ordering: data/ is not excluded as a directory, because git cannot
# re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.las
*.laz
*.ply
*.e57
*.pcd
!data/test/example.las

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Training artefacts
#
# Written by scripts/train.py. The sample directories are the preprocessed
# .npy boxes, regenerated from the training clouds.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/*/sample_dir/
*.npy
model/training_history.csv
model/training_history_permission_error_backup.csv

# model/model.pth (74 MB) is deliberately NOT ignored - the tool cannot run
# without it, and upstream FSCT ships it in-repo too. It is over GitHub's 50 MB
# advisory threshold (under the 100 MB hard limit), so expect a large-file
# warning on push. If that becomes a problem, track it with Git LFS rather than
# dropping it:  git lfs track "model/*.pth"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Misc
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
